{"role":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `CLAUDE.md` file is the repo’s playbook: it explains that `greenlight` is a Go CLI that wraps Claude Code with a PTY + WebSocket relay so the Greenlight server/app can manage sessions. Key subcommands are `connect` (sets up the relay, hooks, and bridge file), `hook` (handles Claude hook events), `stream` (tails transcripts and pushes them to the bridge or HTTP endpoint), `register`, `secrets`, etc.\n\nBuild uses Go 1.24+ and requires `-ldflags` to set `wsURL`/`version`, with cross-platform targets defined for darwin/linux and amd64/arm64. Release scripts live in `scripts/`, and integration tests run via `go test -tags integration`. Conventions include never printing to stdout/stderr during runtime (use `log.Printf`), and several environment variables (`GREENLIGHT_DEVICE_ID/SESSION_ID/PROJECT/BRIDGE`) are injected into child processes by `connect`.\n\n**Preparing response summary**"}]}}